description:
On 2026-11-03 the review broker lost its muse-code login. Nothing alerted. On 2026-11-06 the gateway host script refused to restart (`no broker login for: muse-code`), and every hosted and local review failed closed. The PR removing muse could not be reviewed, because review needs the gateway, so it merged through a 7-second owner-authorized ruleset relaxation (#3965). The cause is structural: hard-coded provider lists in the host script and Theseus `gateway-clients`, accounts required for every provider in the config, no availability-aware reviewer substitution (omp falls back only on usage limits), no outage path in `make pr-open`, and no monitoring. The plan is in local://provider-loss-resilience-plan.md:
- the host derives providers from the trusted config and starts with whichever are logged in, plus an owner-held denylist;
- Theseus selects the first served model from each role's fallback chain and reports substitutions;
- an `unavailable` pending cause that spends no budget;
- a host monitor and an hourly CI health job;
- tests forbidding hard-coded provider requirements.
Sequence: a Theseus release, then a BenchBox lock-only PR, then a BenchBox host/monitor PR.
